lightly Republican given the district's R+4 lean, but the favorable environment, even money, and a knife-edge polling picture offset that. Recent rater movement leans R, so the forecast sits just right of even with wide uncertainty.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling in October or a shift in outside spending could break the tossup either way.", "confidence": "low", "notes": []}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open-seat battle between Republican Casey Askar and Democrat Pia Dandiya in a district that leaned Republican by four points at the last presidential election. Both candidates have raised over $2.2 million, with Dandiya holding a modest cash advantage and benefiting from a gun-safety ad blitz, while outside groups have spent against Askar, whose Jan. 6 positioning has drawn scrutiny.\n\nExpert ratings are genuinely split: Cook, Fox, RCP, and the Economist call it a Tossup, while several October ratings tilt Republican and two outlets lean Democratic. The few available polls, all Democratic-sponsored and dating to August, show a dead heat. Prediction markets price the Democrat at a slim edge. With the national environment favoring Democrats but the district favoring Republicans, this remains one of the closest House races on the board.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5967, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5933, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5824, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.562